        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "15788fa3-901d-5fd5-9f4d-53ff0696367f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Elissa Schappell, Oprah Winfrey, Holly MacArthur, Rob Spillman, Melissa Broder\n- Organizations: Newsweek, The Daily Beast, O, The Oprah Magazine, Hearst Communications, Tin House, Grand Central\n- Products: Last Sext, So Sad Today\n- Topics: magazines, editing, publishing, Twitter\n\nFacts:\n- O, The Oprah Magazine is a monthly magazine founded by Oprah Winfrey and Hearst Communications and is primarily marketed at women.\n- Tin House was developed with the help of New York editors Rob Spillman and Elissa Schappell, and Holly MacArthur served as managing editor.\n- Elissa Schappell is associated with Newsweek/The Daily Beast and O Magazine.\n- Melissa Broder published the poetry collection Last Sext with Tin House in 2016.\n- Melissa Broder published the essay collection So Sad Today with Grand Central in 2016.\n- Melissa Broder also created a popular Twitter feed titled So Sad Today, and the book is based on that feed.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
