        "text": "Page: Elissa Schappell. Sentence: Newsweek/The Daily Beast\", and \"O Magazine\".\nPage: O, The Oprah Magazine. Sentence: O, The Oprah Magazine, sometimes simply abbreviated to O, is a monthly magazine founded by Oprah Winfrey and Hearst Communications, primarily marketed at women.\nPage: Tin House. Sentence: He enlisted Holly MacArthur as managing editor and developed the magazine with the help of two experienced New York editors, Rob Spillman and Elissa Schappell.\nPage: Melissa Broder. Sentence: Her work includes poetry collection \"Last Sext\" (Tin House 2016) and essay collection \"So Sad Today\" (Grand Central 2016), as well as a popular Twitter feed also titled So Sad Today, on which the book is based.",
